       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order. Even with your confirmation, 100 mg of amlodipine daily is a dose I believe would seriously harm this patient. No indication calls for it, and it's well into the range where we'd expect overdose toxicity in a 70 kg adult with normal organ function. I also didn't get a clinical rationale.\n\nI can enter any of these right away:\n\n- **Amlodipine 10 mg** by mouth once daily, the maximum labeled dose\n- **Amlodipine 5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **Amlodipine 2.5 mg** by mouth once daily\n- **An add-on antihypertensive**, if 10 mg isn't controlling the patient's blood pressure. Tell me the agent and dose.\n\nIf there's an unusual circumstance I don't know about, the safer route is to discuss it with pharmacy and enter the order through your institution's override process. That way a second clinician reviews it."
